[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9294"] :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|1\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot 0| \\\\  & =|-2-0| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-316578/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "a5e55e21-f903-510f-9214-855c2cd98385" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186283997 :answer-field/choices ["q-316578/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316570/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "b88fd51e-2eed-5784-ba34-0c3cad89bd12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316570/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "40367811-9a73-5916-b093-a222a0b5a8cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316570/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer-field/choices ["q-316570/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316570" :question/id #uuid "603117f6-d3e5-5477-9c63-84d1378d6081" :question/math-academy-id "q-316570" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|6\\cdot 3-(-10)\\cdot (-5)| \\\\  & =|18-50| \\\\  & =|-32| \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316570/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316569/field-1/0641ac766deb59c60fe7a6b129095b1e1afc9366c5d9d5b56589d495b2595058" :answer/id #uuid "16e1b40d-5e5a-5e30-89c8-edac91f58529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "89" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316569/field-1/931379a785378516de28900bafcfb26ad0864ca12caeba3450580efdd73c93ef" :answer/id #uuid "3831a940-666b-51f6-878e-71b88512ceae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-89" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316569/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "182ce720-e152-57eb-9369-c8490a44193b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316569/field-1/0641ac766deb59c60fe7a6b129095b1e1afc9366c5d9d5b56589d495b2595058" :answer-field/choices ["q-316569/field-1/0641ac766deb59c60fe7a6b129095b1e1afc9366c5d9d5b56589d495b2595058" "q-316569/field-1/931379a785378516de28900bafcfb26ad0864ca12caeba3450580efdd73c93ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316569" :question/id #uuid "182ce155-065c-526e-891c-1c2103b06de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316569" :question/problem "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." :question/worked-solution "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-10\\cdot 8-9\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|-80-9| \\\\  & =|-89| \\\\  & =89.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316569/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80a4eee7-a763-5c28-ae3c-5bce78222c87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316569"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316591/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "b9767f93-7e87-508f-bcf9-fd3a7cebce9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284005 :answer-field/choices ["q-316591/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-316591"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/455e0a08e2a0929a60d7fa1b76973e1b7a460efe8cc1cf01719ce211feacd8c0.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-316585/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "c4403f15-4d99-556e-baff-d5374b2c5b43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316585/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c91ff50-1701-5eb5-9b4f-99237b8d8226" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316585/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer-field/choices ["q-316585/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316585" :question/id #uuid "e7cbbaf2-6a2c-5981-8af6-1993d3e9c447" :question/math-academy-id "q-316585" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/7edace8cab645caab8309768ede92f534281567640aba7082f647ca1c8a49074.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,3\\,|\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316585/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316584/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316584/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "376b8af6-29bc-55ae-be7a-9659c2559891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316584/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1965bafe-8660-507f-9547-8ea44caad029" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316584/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-316584/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-316584/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316584" :question/id #uuid "b9258d52-01b3-55d0-afcb-ea66a3cfa2e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-316584" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316584/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316584"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "300a3c35-9bdc-526e-a0e2-a3e1c6d3da61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "bf97bd72-0294-51d9-9663-7987a2190c25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309/selection/728ecd05f971a253a3c26dbe75d9e0a7cfee71804ca75ebb83455b35d611b45b" :answer/id #uuid "b1a00c06-8cc0-5ba1-9c02-5af4e0877c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "66" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309/selection/14fdd9c68b8f5cd541a0350dfd956e125452e735121bf2c13030d9ba47197cf0" :answer/id #uuid "63131879-2b6e-5b83-83dd-a031a832723b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-66" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "8ff9ee8f-390b-513b-9a00-66b2db1dd708" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1d90599-afa5-593e-84e0-cb850f9e6efe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9309/selection/728ecd05f971a253a3c26dbe75d9e0a7cfee71804ca75ebb83455b35d611b45b" :answer-field/choices ["q-9309/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-9309/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-9309/selection/728ecd05f971a253a3c26dbe75d9e0a7cfee71804ca75ebb83455b35d611b45b" "q-9309/selection/14fdd9c68b8f5cd541a0350dfd956e125452e735121bf2c13030d9ba47197cf0" "q-9309/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9309" :question/id #uuid "c827fba0-90ed-5026-9ebc-6dd1e8034231" :question/math-academy-id "q-9309" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/bd50e99a129b1d6a2c6b73145dbf68681bc92a3cef0ca8e743b63cf96c9afafc.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (2+4)=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-1)=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,11\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-9309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275984/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "703055c3-5adb-52ba-9b8f-272da61ca0ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275984/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "38ca7b73-7efb-5dea-a3ab-7fc323a6825f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275984/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-275984/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275984" :question/id #uuid "48ced98e-b54b-5c6a-b9fb-ebded7bc7e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-275984" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/32fc2965c35872f2511ab7c24e931d62c8cbcc6d1c70c67cad6016dedad5d8fd.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=0\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275984/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316607/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "042bfcba-1272-5a6d-b6f0-b3e1d9655a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284012 :answer-field/choices ["q-316607/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-316607"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/059560835586e9c149cdb5dabcddc80610a58bfa0c30cb5f685b8bb6bdca3e90.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 5=15.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-316606"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/3e2c56766f201095bee0eea101b877e30910c676c998f37d261fd7cf7aabb837.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-316601/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "a36cd622-9700-5d2a-98fd-764e0be6bc9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316601/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "04113139-bdaf-5a64-9ae1-649d8e783b69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316601/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a6df28c-19d0-5a33-9a46-56de57b84f98" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316601/field-1/713bb3b087